# Gate Test - BONANZA's SWITCHES, KEYS, GATES and DRAWBRIDGE test course (SPEC.md 130.41), built only by the
# BZGATE=1 knob (make BUILD=<tree> BZGATE=1 bonanzadisk).  NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES
# and makes it the pathway's pad 0, so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.
# A PLATE (rolled over) or a KEY (touched) opens its CHANNEL for the attempt: every gate of it opens and every
# bridge of it comes down.  Each channel is its GLYPH, black on white, on all of its elements.
#
# START is a plate at 2 units with a pad for each ball and two switch plates (RING, BOX).  From it:
#  - east, the RING GATE (wy 8 - 9): a corridor shut by two ring gates until the ring plate is rolled over;
#    a goal (exit 1) behind them;
#  - south, the KEY GATE (wx 9 - 10): a lane shut by two plus gates; the PLUS KEY waits in a nook beside it;
#    a goal behind them;
#  - south-east, the TIMED DRAWBRIDGE (wy 11 - 12): six cells over the void, down 128 steps in every 256 (2.3 s each way);
#    caught up, the ball falls; a goal across it;
#  - west, the BOX DRAWBRIDGE (wy 10 - 11): two cells up until the box plate is rolled over; a goal across it.
# THE ART's STYLES (SPEC.md 130.41.11), one an element group: the ring gates CRYSTAL, the plus gates PORTCULLIS,
# the timed drawbridge's deck PICKET (planks), the box drawbridge the default GRILLE (its plain seam).
course GATE "Gate Test"
music fairway    # a test course: SPEC.md 130.50.3, every course names its song
width  128
origin 320
ball   rubber

uses gate

floor rect 8 8 14 14 flat 2   # the start plate
pad rubber 9 9
pad steel 10 9
pad glass 11 9
start 10 11
prop plate 12 12 channel ring
prop plate 9 13 channel box

# THE RING GATE: the corridor east, its two gates, a goal behind them
floor rect 14 8 24 10 flat 2
prop gate 18 8 channel ring along x style crystal
prop gate 18 9 channel ring along x style crystal
goal tile 22 8 flat 2 exit 1

# THE KEY GATE: the lane south, its two gates; the key's nook beside it; a goal behind them
floor rect 9 14 11 24 flat 2
floor rect 11 15 13 17 flat 2
prop key 12 16 channel plus
prop gate 9 19 channel plus along y style portcullis
prop gate 10 19 channel plus along y style portcullis
goal tile 9 22 flat 2

# THE TIMED DRAWBRIDGE: six thin cells over the void, down 128 steps of every 256
floor rect 14 11 24 13 flat 2
float rect 16 11 19 13 thick 0.5
prop bridge 16 11 19 13 period 256 on 128 style picket
goal tile 22 12 flat 2

# THE BOX DRAWBRIDGE: two thin cells, up until the box plate is rolled over
floor rect 3 10 8 12 flat 2
float rect 6 10 7 12 thick 0.5
prop bridge 6 10 7 12 channel box
goal tile 4 11 flat 2

target 60
way 10 11
way 12 11
way 12 9
way 21 9

# THE ART GATES (SPEC.md 130.41.12): three short corridors north of the start plate, each shut by a gate of the
# designer's own ART (apps/bonanza/courses/gates/*.bba, four frames shut to open), into a back hall with a goal.
# Each opens with a channel the presets use, so the preset scenes play the art's frames as well:
#  - x 8, the DOOR (box): a door frame and a plank door that swings open away from the viewer;
#  - x 10, the CRUMBLE (ring): a brick wall between two blocks that cracks, crumbles and falls to rubble;
#  - x 12 - 13, the PORTCULLIS (plus): a stone arch over two cells, its iron grid rising into it.
floor rect 8 3 14 6 flat 2     # the back hall (wy 3 - 4) and the gates' row (wy 5)
floor rect 8 6 9 8 flat 2      # the door's corridor
floor rect 10 6 11 8 flat 2    # the crumble's
floor rect 12 6 14 8 flat 2    # the portcullis's, two cells wide
wall tile 9 5 flat 3           # the crumble's two blocks, a unit proud
wall tile 11 5 flat 3
prop gate 8 5 channel box along y art door
prop gate 10 5 channel ring along y art crumble
prop plate 10 6 channel ring   # (a second ring plate, right before the wall: the ball waits while it crumbles)
prop gate 12 5 channel plus along y art portcullis
goal tile 10 3 flat 2
